      "payload": "{\"messages\":[{\"content\":[{\"id\":\"client:c_3002\",\"text\":\"<client id=\\\"client:c_3002\\\">\\nClient Kwame Asante (c_3002): self-directed mandate, growth risk tier, KYC verified, country GB.\\n</client>\\n\"},{\"id\":\"ledger:acct_7702\",\"text\":\"<account id=\\\"ledger:acct_7702\\\">\\nLedger for the account as of 2026-10-06T08:30:00Z: cash 3100.00 GBP. Positions: ACME (Acme Industrial plc): 1000 units settled, average cost 40.75; NIMB (Nimbus Data): 80 units settled, average cost 215.00.\\n</account>\\n\"},{\"id\":\"risk:s_c3_05\",\"text\":\"<account id=\\\"risk:s_c3_05\\\">\\nRisk screen for this session: critical. Signals: session from a device this account has not used before; the message names an amount of 5,000 or more; the message asks about moving money.\\n</account>\\n\"},{\"id\":\"contract:triage\",\"text\":\"<format id=\\\"contract:triage\\\">\\nReply as JSON with exactly these keys: \\\"summary\\\" (plain text for the client, at most 120 words), \\\"urgency\\\" (one of: low, normal, high, critical), \\\"team\\\" (one of: fraud, disputes, access, general), \\\"citations\\\" (the list of article paragraph ids you relied on), \\\"actions\\\" (a list, possibly empty, of {\\\"tool\\\", \\\"arguments\\\"} objects using only the tools you were offered). No other keys, no text outside the JSON.\\n</format>\\n\"},{\"id\":\"quote:ACME\",\"text\":\"<market id=\\\"quote:ACME\\\">\\nLast quote ACME: 42.10 GBP at 2026-10-06T08:58:00Z (vendor feed, may be delayed).\\n</market>\\n\"},{\"id\":\"quote:NIMB\",\"text\":\"<market id=\\\"quote:NIMB\\\">\\nLast quote NIMB: 198.40 GBP at 2026-10-06T08:58:00Z (vendor feed, may be delayed).\\n</market>\\n\"},{\"id\":\"kb:fees-and-charges@3#1\",\"text\":\"<article id=\\\"kb:fees-and-charges@3#1\\\">\\nCustody is charged at 0.10% a year on all accounts. There is no charge for holding cash, and no exit fee on transfers out of the platform.\\n</article>\\n\"},{\"id\":\"kb:fraud-and-disputes@5#0\",\"text\":\"<article id=\\\"kb:fraud-and-disputes@5#0\\\">\\nA client who reports a transfer or payment they did not make is treated as a suspected fraud report. Open a case for the fraud team at high urgency, and stop any pending outbound transfer on the account until the team has spoken to the client.\\n</article>\\n\"},{\"id\":\"kb:fraud-and-disputes@5#1\",\"text\":\"<article id=\\\"kb:fraud-and-disputes@5#1\\\">\\nA report from a device the account has not used before, or within 24 hours of a credential change, is escalated to critical urgency.\\n</article>\\n\"},{\"id\":\"kb:suitability-and-mandates@2#1\",\"text\":\"<article id=\\\"kb:suitability-and-mandates@2#1\\\">\\nA self-directed mandate means the client places their own orders. The assistant may queue an order for the client to confirm when the account's risk screen is clear.\\n</article>\\n\"},{\"id\":\"turn:s_c3_05:0001\",\"text\":\"<message id=\\\"turn:s_c3_05:0001\\\">\\nI didn't make this transfer of 9,800 to an account I don't recognise. What is going on?\\n</message>\\n\"}],\"role\":\"user\"}],\"system\":[{\"id\":\"policy:triage\",\"text\":\"You are the Larkbridge Wealth service triage assistant. A client has reported a problem. From the client profile, the risk screen, the articles and the conversation, classify the report and route it to the right team.\\n\\nUrgency is never lower than the risk screen's level. A transaction the client did not make is fraud at high urgency, critical when the risk screen is elevated. You do not move money, freeze anything or decide whether fraud occurred; you open the case with an open_case action in actions, naming the team's category, and explain what happens next. A summary alone opens nothing. Never include an account number, IBAN or card number in your reply. Cite the article paragraph id for every rule you apply.\"}],\"tools\":[{\"id\":\"cap:open_case\",\"text\":\"{\\\"description\\\": \\\"Open a service case for the fraud, disputes, access or general team.\\\", \\\"input_schema\\\": {\\\"additionalProperties\\\": false, \\\"properties\\\": {\\\"category\\\": {\\\"enum\\\": [\\\"fraud\\\", \\\"dispute\\\", \\\"access\\\", \\\"general\\\"], \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, \\\"client\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}}, \\\"required\\\": [\\\"client\\\", \\\"category\\\"], \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\"}, \\\"name\\\": \\\"open_case\\\"}\"}]}"
